 "capsule": "Han (韓) was one of the Seven Warring States of ancient China, formed in 453 BC when the ministerial Han, Wei, and Zhao families partitioned the state of Jin, with Han's independence formally recognized by the Zhou king in 403 BC. Hemmed in by Qin, Chu, Qi, and Wei across a mountainous stretch of southern Shanxi and central Henan, Han was the smallest and most vulnerable of the seven states, despite administrative reforms under chancellor Shen Buhai. It became the first of the seven to fall to Qin's unification campaigns, conquered in 230 BC — an ancient Chinese state wholly unrelated to the medieval Anatolian Beylik of Saruhan, more than fifteen centuries its junior.",
